From: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos990: add pd_csis power domain

Add the CSIS (camera MIPI-CSI2) power domain node at 0x15861d80 with
its SMC ID (0x17010204) from downstream exynos9830-pm-domains.dtsi.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@local>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
index 000000000..000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
@@ -956,6 +956,16 @@
 			label = "G3D";
 		};
 
+		/* CSIS (camera MIPI-CSI2) power domain. PMU @0x15860000 + 0x1d80;
+		 * downstream "pd-csis" with need_smc = 0x17010204. */
+		pd_csis: power-domain@15861d80 {
+			compatible = "samsung,exynos990-pd";
+			reg = <0x15861d80 0x20>;
+			samsung,need-smc = <0x17010204>;
+			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			label = "CSIS";
+		};
+
 		/* AUD (audio/ABOX) power domain. PMU @0x15860000 + 0x1900; downstream
 		 * "pd-aud" (config reg 0x15861900, status +0x1904, mask 0x1). If the
 		 * PMU cannot power it the exynos-pd poll just times out (no hang) and
-- 
2.47.0
